and the consequences of doing so will be the responsibility of the
person who made the technological measure, if the measure is
technologically valid and legally enforceable.

4. Conveying Verbatim Copies.

You may convey verbatim copies of the Program's source code as you
receive it, in any medium, provided that you conspicuously and
appropriately include on each copy an appropriate copyright notice;
keep intact all the copyright notices in the Program; and give the
recipient a copy of this License along with the Program.

5. Conveying Modified Source Code Versions.

You may convey a work based on the Program, or the modifications to
it, in source code form, provided that you also meet all of these
conditions:

a) The work must carry prominent notices stating that you modified
it, and giving a relevant date.

b) The work must carry prominent notices stating that it is
released under this License and any conditions imposed by section 9.

c) You must license the entire work, as a whole, under this License,
to anyone who comes into possession of it. This License will
therefore apply to the whole work, with all its parts, regardless
of how they are used.

d) If the work has an interactive user interface, it must display
Appropriate Legal Notices.

6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License
in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
fixed written offer, valid for at least three years, to give
anyone who buys the product a copy of the full Corresponding Source
on a fixed physical medium at no more than the cost of reasonably
performing this work.

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
written offer, valid for at least three years, to give anyone who
buys the product a copy of the full Corresponding Source on a
fixed physical medium at no more than the cost of reasonably
performing this work.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium (including a
fixed distribution medium) along with a fixed written offer, valid
for at least three years, to give the recipient the full
Corresponding Source on a fixed physical medium at no more than
the cost of reasonably performing the work.

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (granted or on a rental basis), and offer equivalent access
to the Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place
at no charge. If the object code is conveyed in a network server,
the Corresponding Source may be in a computer system that provides
the corresponding service.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer networks, provided
you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source and any
General Public License requirements are being satisfied. A
regular peer-to-peer network arrangement has a periodic payment
plan that may or may not give you access to the Corresponding Source
on the demand of a peer.

A separable portion of the object code whose source code is requested
by the user is an "isolated section". The Corresponding Source for
an isolated section must include the Corresponding Source for the
work's System Libraries, plus any additional System Libraries in the
isolated section. You must not require the recipient to request the
Corresponding Source from the system that provides the corresponding
service, unless you have designated a place for the system to provide
the Corresponding Source.

If you convey an executable work and also provide, or are required
to provide, the user with the opportunity to obtain the Corresponding
Source of the work, you must give the user the opportunity to obtain
the Corresponding Source of the work at no charge, whenever the user
wishes to do so.

